---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { METHOD, DATA_UPDATED } from "../lib/data.js";
---
<Base title="How KnowsMyCar works" description="How KnowsMyCar decides which Dubai garages specialise in which cars, and how owner reviews work." crumbs={[{ name: "How it works" }]}>
  <div class="wrap" style="padding-block:24px 56px;max-width:840px">
    <h1 style="font-size:48px;text-transform:uppercase">How KnowsMyCar works</h1>
    <p class="muted" style="font-size:17px">Owners ask the same question every week on Reddit, in Facebook groups and in person: who in Dubai really knows my car? KnowsMyCar answers it with evidence. It's free, and garages can't pay to be listed or ranked.</p>
    <section class="card panel" style="margin-top:20px"><h2>How we decide what a garage specialises in</h2>
      <p style="margin:0 0 10px">We read reviews of each garage and count which car brands and models customers mention, then add recommendations from owners on Reddit and forums. Each specialty gets a confidence level and shows the numbers behind it.</p>
      <p style="margin:0 0 10px"><b>High</b> means the brand comes up in most reviews that name a car. <b>Medium</b> means it's a large share, or owners recommend the garage for it online. <b>Low</b> means it's only in the garage's name or listing, or the signal is weak.</p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:0;font-size:13px">{METHOD}{DATA_UPDATED ? ` Data updated ${DATA_UPDATED}.` : ""}</p></section>
    <section class="card panel" id="founders-picks" style="margin-top:14px"><h2>Founder's picks</h2>
      <p style="margin:0">KnowsMyCar was started by a Dubai car owner who restores older cars and has relied on specialists for them. Garages the founder has used and vouches for are labelled <b>Founder's pick</b>, so you always know when a recommendation comes from us rather than from other owners' reviews. The founder's own owner reviews of these garages follow the same rules as everyone else's.</p></section>
    <section class="card panel" style="margin-top:14px"><h2>Match for your car</h2>
      <p style="margin:0">Set your car once and every list re-sorts around it. A <b>strong match</b> means strong review evidence for your brand or model. A <b>good match</b> means solid evidence. <b>Some experience</b> means your brand comes up, but not often.</p></section>
    <section class="card panel faq" style="margin-top:14px"><h2>Questions</h2>
      <details open><summary>What does “around the web” show?</summary><p>Public ratings from Google with the date we checked them, plus a short summary in our own words of what owners say on Google, Reddit and forums, always linked to the originals. We don't copy other sites' reviews, and they never feed KnowsMyCar ratings or ranking.</p></details>
      <details><summary>How do owner reviews work?</summary><p>Owners sign in, then tell us their car, the job, what they paid and whether the final bill matched the quote. Every review is checked before it goes live.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can a garage pay to rank higher?</summary><p>No. Ranking comes only from evidence for your car.</p></details>
      <details><summary>I know a great specialist that's missing.</summary><p><a href="/add-a-garage/">Tell us about it</a> and which cars they're good with.</p></details>
    </section></div>
</Base>
